    <string name="train_share_terms_title">Share with everyone?</string>
    <string name="train_share_terms_body">Anyone using Med Herb Lens will be able to find this model, add it and train it further.\n\n• It’s shared under the Creative Commons Attribution licence (CC BY 4.0), and, unless you untick it when sharing, also published on Hugging Face, where anyone can download it.\n• It includes its name, the species names you typed and a compact summary of your photos that lets it go on learning. Your photos themselves aren’t included, nor your name or email.\n• Don’t use people’s names, contact details or anything offensive. Shared models can be reported, and we remove those that break the terms of service.\n• You can stop sharing it at any time, which removes it from Hugging Face too; copies others already added stay with them.</string>
    <string name="train_share_accept">Agree and share</string>
    <string name="train_share_confirm_title">Share with everyone?</string>
    <string name="train_share_confirm_body">Anyone using Med Herb Lens will be able to add it to their models and train it further.</string>
    <string name="train_share_hf">Also publish it on Hugging Face (recommended)</string>
    <string name="train_share_hf_body">It’s published at once in the Med Herb Lens organisation on Hugging Face, where researchers look for models, with a page that credits Med Herb Lens users, not you by name. It helps the research reach more people.</string>
